  <p>
    <code>reelSet.runCascade(options)</code> (<code>core/ReelSet.ts</code>)
    takes the two callbacks from the figure, <code>detectWinners</code> and <code>nextGrid</code>, the optional hooks <code>presentWinners</code> and <code>onCascade</code>, and the knobs <code>pauseAfterDestroyMs</code>, <code>maxChain</code>, <code>destroyOptions</code>, <code>refillMode</code>, <code>gravityHoldMs</code>, <code>gravityHold</code>, <code>onGravityComplete</code> and <code>signal</code>. The round's
    signal is forwarded to <code>destroySymbols</code> unless <code>destroyOptions</code> carries its own; a <code>gravityHold</code> given as a function is invoked at gravity end; and the loop checks <code>wasSkipped</code> after every await. After each refill it reads
    the board back with <code>getVisibleGrid()</code> to feed the next <code>detectWinners</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    For one stage, the events arrive in this order: <code>cascade:chain:start</code>, <code>cascade:destroy:start</code>, <code>cascade:destroy:end</code>, <code>spin:start</code> (from the
    refill), then per reel <code>cascade:place:end</code>, <code>cascade:dropIn:start</code>, the <code>:symbol</code> events and <code>cascade:dropIn:end</code> (with the gravity events first in
    two-stage mode) and <code>spin:reelLanding</code> / <code>spin:reelLanded</code>, then <code>spin:allLanded</code>, <code>spin:complete</code> and <code>cascade:chain:end</code>. The <a href="/architecture/events/">events page</a> has every payload.
  </p>

  <p>
    <code>refill</code> checks everything before it changes any state: the
    grid shape, v1 keys and buffer counts (<code>_assertGrid</code>), that no
    spin or refill is in flight, that <code>.tumble()</code> was configured,
    that the column count and visible length match the reels, and that every
    winner is in range. Only then does it take the spinning state, set the
    spin mode to <code>'cascade'</code>, build all the frames up front, group
    the winners per reel in ascending order and emit <code>spin:start</code>.
    A failure in stage 1 or in the hold of <code>'gravity-then-drop'</code> emits <code>cascade:gravity:error {`{ error }`}</code>, logs, and slams.
    From reading the code, <code>refill()</code> emits <code>spin:start</code> and <code>spin:allLanded</code>, so pin turns and <code>'eval'</code> pins are probably spent on every refill; that has not
    been tested.
  </p>

